}

{
  "summary": "P1 security ticket EVAL-sec-03. Aisha Khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, New York, usual hours 09:00-17:00, Duo push enrolled on phone) reports she clicked a link in a payroll verification email and typed her password on the page before realizing. Time of click and the sender/subject of the email are not stated in the ticket. Checked: account is active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, must_change_password false. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days (10 sign-ins, VPN and M365, all New York, residential or corporate IPs, all Duo push, all within usual hours, 0 hosting-network sign-ins, 0 failed passwords, 0 MFA denials) show nothing suspicious. Action taken: reset_password queued for technician approval (approval id 1); not yet run. Not blocked, since logs show no misuse. Needed: technician to verify user by callback and deliver the temporary password by phone only; confirm the click time with the user and recheck sign-ins after it; obtain the phishing email (sender, subject, payroll verification request) for security review and check whether other users received it.",
  "reason": "KB-029 requires escalation for any credential-entry on a phishing site. P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Thanks for reporting this right away, Aisha. Please do the following now: don't delete the payroll email, since the security team needs it to review the sender. Don't click that link again or type your password anywhere else. Don't approve any Duo push you did not start yourself. If you opened any attachment from that email, disconnect from Wi-Fi and tell us. A password reset has been requested and is waiting for a technician to approve it. Once approved, a technician will call you to verify your identity and give you a temporary password by phone. Please don't wait on that call to tell us when you clicked the link, since it helps us check your account activity. Security has also been notified and will follow up.",
  "internal_note": "P1, KB-029 and KB-008. User aisha.khan (user_id 5, HR, NY, Duo push enrolled). Account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins. Sign-in logs for 14 days show 10 normal sign-ins (VPN and M365, NY residential or corporate IPs, Duo push, within usual hours, no hosting networks, no failed passwords, no MFA denials), so no evidence of misuse yet. Click time not given, so logs cannot be correlated to it. reset_password queued as approval id 1, not run. block_sign_in not requested because logs show no misuse; a technician may choose to block if the click time turns up suspicious activity. Escalated as escalation id 1 with full summary. Still needed: callback verification before the temp password is given by phone; the phishing email's sender and subject for security; a check for other recipients.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-029",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
